    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114247" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χνόη</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χνοίη</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>axle-box, nave,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄξων ἐν χνοίῃσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					1.6
				</span></i>
			; prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				46
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλακον ἀξόνων βριθομένων χνόαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					153
				</span></i>
			 (lyr); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθραυσε δ᾽ ἄξονος μέσας χνόας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					745
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				717
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντύγων χνόας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					118
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χνόαι ποδῶν</span>
			<i>the joints</i> on which the feet play, as the wheels on the
			axle, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				371
			</span></i>.</div>
